---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";

// Keep this page true. If the site starts collecting anything new (analytics,
// a form, a store), update the relevant section and the date below.
const updated = new Date("2026-09-14");
const fmt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric" });
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site does and does not collect about you.">
  <article class="pt-10 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="max-w-[60ch]">
      <h1 class="text-[2rem] leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-[2.75rem]">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[1.125rem] text-muted">
        The short version: this site does not track you. Here is the long version.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.875rem] text-muted">
        Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString()}>{fmt.format(updated)}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-12">
      <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        madebyanirudha.in is a personal site run by Anirudha, an individual, not a company. For anything on this
        page, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site collects</h2>
      <p>Nothing, by design.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cookies.</strong> The site sets none and needs none.</li>
        <li><strong>No analytics or tracking.</strong> No Google Analytics, no pixels, no fingerprinting, no third-party scripts.</li>
        <li><strong>No accounts or forms.</strong> There is nothing to sign up for and nothing to fill in.</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party fonts or embeds.</strong> Fonts are served from this domain. Photographs and drawings are hosted here.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Your browser may keep its own copy of pages and images in its cache so they load faster next time. That is
        your browser's behaviour, on your device, and you control it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a>. To deliver pages
        and to block abuse, Cloudflare processes the technical details of each request: your IP address, the page
        requested, the time, your browser's user-agent string, and the country the request came from. Cloudflare's
        handling of that data is described in its own <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I can see aggregate traffic numbers and short-lived request logs in the Cloudflare dashboard. I use them only to
        keep the site up and to notice when something is broken. I do not export them, combine them with anything
        else, or share them.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me, I will have your email address and whatever you wrote. I keep it in my mailbox for as long
        as the conversation is useful, and I do not add you to any list. Ask, and I will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other places</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to my accounts on Instagram, YouTube and Instructables, and occasionally to other sites in
        guides and build logs. Once you follow a link you are on their site, under their policies. I do not embed
        their players or widgets here, so simply reading this site sends nothing to them.
      </p>

      <h2>When the store opens</h2>
      <p>
        I plan to sell some of the things I make. When that happens, checkout will run through a payment provider, and
        an order will necessarily involve your name, delivery address, and payment details handled by that provider.
        This page will be updated before the store goes live to say exactly who is involved and what is kept.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Whatever the law in your country calls them, the practical version is: you can ask what I have about you (for
        almost everyone, the answer is nothing), ask me to delete it, or ask a question. Email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If anything above changes, this page changes with it and the date at the top moves. There is no separate
        notice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
